---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import ComponentPreview from "../../../components/ComponentPreview.astro";
import { dialogConfirmScript, dialogConfirmTree, dialogVaulScript, dialogVaulTree } from "../../../demos/dialog";
import { getLocale, useTranslations } from "../../../i18n";
import StylingHooks from "../../../components/StylingHooks.astro";

const t = useTranslations(getLocale(Astro.url));

const install = `pnpm add @skryensya/core`;

const styles = `@import "@skryensya/core/components/dialog.css";
@import "@skryensya/core/patterns/scroll-lock.css";`;


const confirmJs = `const dialog = document.getElementById("confirm-delete");
const trigger = document.querySelector(
  '[data-dialog-open="confirm-delete"]',
);

trigger?.addEventListener("click", () => {
  if (dialog instanceof HTMLDialogElement) dialog.showModal();
});

// Optional: read which button closed the form.
dialog?.addEventListener("close", () => {
  console.log(dialog.returnValue); // "cancel" | "confirm"
});`;

const vaulInstall = `pnpm add @skryensya/core @skryensya/vanilla`;

const vaulStyles = `@import "@skryensya/core/components/dialog.css";
@import "@skryensya/core/patterns/dialog-vaul.css";
@import "@skryensya/core/patterns/scroll-lock.css";`;

const vaulJs = `import { initComponents } from "@skryensya/vanilla/auto";

await initComponents();`;
---

<Base
  title="Dialog"
  description="The centered dialogue of the platform. Optional: Dialog Vaul when content requests a surface from the edge on mobile."
>
  <h1>Dialog</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A centered <code>&lt;dialog class="sk-dialog"&gt;</code>. <code>showModal()</code> provides focus, Escape, inert page and backdrop; The system paints the surface. No enhancer: the only JavaScript is to open.
  </p>

  <h2>Confirm</h2>
  <p>
    Anatomy: <code>sk-dialog__header</code> (title with <code>Heading</code> + <code>sk-dialog__title</code>, and closure), <code>sk-dialog__body</code> and <code>sk-dialog__footer</code> (controls). The closure and footer are <code>&lt;form method="dialog"&gt;</code>: they close without a handler and leave the <code>value</code> in <code>dialog.returnValue</code>.
  </p>
  <ComponentPreview tree={dialogConfirmTree(t)} previewScript={dialogConfirmScript} label="Confirm" viewport="overlay" />

  <h2>Opening it</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={confirmJs} label="JavaScript" />

  <h2>Focus and keyboard</h2>
  <p>
    With <code>showModal()</code>, the platform already does the work. Do not reimplement a focus trap
    in JavaScript (decision 11 / WCAG technique H102).
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>When opening</strong> the focus enters the dialog. Without <code>autofocus</code>, land on the first focusable control. In a destructive commit put <code>autofocus</code> in <strong>Cancel</strong> (the safe option), not in Delete or shutdown.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Order in the DOM</strong>: the title goes <em>before</em> of the close button. If the closure were the first focusable node and the content was long, <code>showModal()</code> could open the panel already scrolled to that control.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tab / Shift+Tab</strong> cycle between dialog controls. The page behind is <code>inert</code>: it does not receive focus. Yes you can reach the chrome browser (address bar); That is intentional, not a bug.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Escape</strong> closes the dialog (the <code>cancel</code> event) and restores focus to the trigger. It is equivalent to discarding, not confirming: the same empty/cancel <code>returnValue</code>
      as the close button with <code>value="cancel"</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>When closing</strong> the focus returns to the element that opened the dialog, if it is still on the page. There is no need to keep it on hand.
    </li>
    <li>
      The close button is a <code>sk-button</code> with <code>data-icon-only</code> and <code>aria-label="Close"</code>. The icon is decorative (<code>&lt;span data-sk-icon="close"&gt;</code>); the name belongs to the button.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} label="terminal" />
  <CodeBlock code={styles} label="CSS" lang="css" />

  <h2>Contract</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Opens a <code>&lt;dialog class="sk-dialog"&gt;</code> with <code>showModal()</code>, not a <code>div</code> with role models.
    </li>
    <li>
      Anatomy: <code>sk-dialog__header</code> ( <code>sk-heading sk-dialog__title</code> + <code>sk-dialog__close</code>), <code>sk-dialog__body</code>, <code>sk-dialog__footer</code> (controls, optional). The title is <a class="sk-link sk-interactive" href="/en/components/heading">Heading</a> (almost always with <code>data-flush</code>).
    </li>
    <li>
      Associates the title with <code>aria-labelledby</code> pointing to the <code>id</code> of the Heading (or an equivalent accessible name).
    </li>
    <li>
      Closing and actions use <code>&lt;form method="dialog"&gt;</code>; <code>value</code> on each button if you need to know which one was chosen.
    </li>
    <li>
      Do not add your own focus trap: <code>showModal()</code> already contains the focus and restores on close.
    </li>
    <li>
      Import <a class="sk-link sk-interactive" href="/en/scroll-lock">scroll lock</a> if you want to freeze the page behind without CLS when the scrollbar disappears.
    </li>
    <li>
      With <a class="sk-link sk-interactive" href="/en/transparency"><code>prefers-reduced-transparency</code></a>, the backdrop leaves the mix translucent and becomes an opaque background; The modality does not change.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Option: Dialog Vaul</h2>
  <p>
    When the content requests a surface from the edge on mobile, the same <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> can opt in <strong>Dialog Vaul</strong>: adds slide, light-dismiss and drag-to-dismiss. The mode (focus, Escape, inert) remains <code>showModal()</code>.
  </p>
  <ComponentPreview tree={dialogVaulTree(t)} previewScript={dialogVaulScript} label="Dialog Vaul" viewport="overlay" />

  <h3>What</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Open and close with authorized triggers and closers (<code>data-sk-dialog-vaul-open</code> /
      <code>-close</code>).</li>
    <li>adds Below <code>52rem</code>, let the handle be dragged towards <code>block-end</code>.</li>
    <li>Light-dismiss when pressing outside the panel rectangle.</li>
    <li>
      <code>data-sk-dialog-vaul</code> opts for the improvement; <code>data-edge="block-end"</code> names the edge. The handle is optional.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Install Dialog Vaul</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={vaulInstall} label="terminal" />
  <CodeBlock code={vaulStyles} label="CSS" lang="css" />
  <CodeBlock code={vaulJs} label="JavaScript" />

  <h2>The border always on is not aesthetic</h2>
  <p>
    In high contrast the panel and the page resolve to the same color: softening <code>--sk-dialog-border-width</code> leaves the dialog invisible without failing a single test. That is why it arrives in <code>1px</code> and not in <code>0</code>.
  </p>

  <StylingHooks
    groups={[
      { file: "components/dialog.css", probe: "sk-dialog", title: "Dialog" },
      { file: "patterns/dialog-vaul.css", probe: "data-sk-dialog-vaul", title: "Dialog Vaul" },
    ]}
  />
</Base>

